# Comedy App Backend Platform Architecture Plan

## Objective

Design and implement a production-ready backend platform for a comedy discovery application.

The platform enables:

- Fans to discover comedy clips and events
- Fans to follow comedians and venues
- Comedians and venues to publish promotional content
- Venues to create events and attach comedians
- Fans to purchase tickets from discovered content (future phase)
- Creators to access analytics about performance and audience behaviour

The system must initially support:

- 10,000+ concurrent users
- Smooth TikTok-style video browsing
- Location-aware discovery
- High-quality recommendations
- Creator analytics
- Future scalability into millions of users

The architecture should begin as a **modular monolith** using Python/FastAPI but be designed so individual domains can later become microservices.

---

# Architectural Principles

## Core Principles

The backend must:

- Own all business logic
- Keep frontend geographically ignorant
- Avoid coupling to Supabase-specific functionality
- Be event-driven where appropriate
- Use asynchronous processing for expensive operations
- Separate content creation from content distribution
- Optimize for read-heavy workloads

The architecture should support future migration:
