Instructions For Implementation Agent
The implementation agent should:
Preserve modular boundaries.
Avoid premature microservices.
Keep business logic independent from Supabase.
Use repository/service patterns.
Use async workers for expensive operations.
Design every table with future scaling in mind.
Build APIs that can later become service boundaries.
Prioritize feed performance and creator analytics as core competitive advantages.
The final system should behave like a professional consumer discovery platform comparable in architecture quality to modern video/social platforms while remaining appropriate for an early-stage startup.




